
 Brief Summary
The plusOne method adds 1 to a number represented as an array of digits.

It starts from the last digit and moves left.
If adding 1 doesn't cause a carry, it updates the digit and returns.
If it becomes 10, it sets the digit to 0 and continues (carry forward).
If all digits are 9, it creates a new array with an extra digit (e.g., [9,9] → [1,0,0]).


⏱️ Time Complexity

O(n) → In the worst case, it traverses all digits (e.g., [9,9,9]).


📦 Space Complexity

O(1) → No extra space in most cases
O(n) → When a new array is created (all digits are 9)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public int[] plusOne(int[] digits) {
        for(int i=digits.length-1;i>=0;i--){
            if(digits[i]+1!=10){
                digits[i]+=1;
                return digits;
            }
            digits[i]=0;
        }
        int[] newDigits= new int[digits.length+1];
        newDigits[0]=1;
        return newDigits;

        
    }
}
